          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The definition of a
            %strong Gorenstein
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            is motivated by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gorenstein+ring"} Gorenstein condition
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+ring"} Noetherian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local ring
            such that the
            = succeed "-group" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ext"} Ext
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ext
                    %mi R
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext^{\ast}_R(k, R)
            is one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            as a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/residue+field"} residue field
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            of the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"}> right derived
            ) Hom complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_R(k, R)
            is equivalent to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            Thus, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R} \to \mathbf{k}
            is said to be Gorenstein if there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi a
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\mathbf{R}}(\mathbf{k}, \mathbf{R}) \simeq \Sigma^a\mathbf{k}
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
          %p
            A ring,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gorenstein+ring"} Gorenstein
            if and only if the ring spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R \to H k
            is Gorenstein.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Examples from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+stable+homotopy+theory"} chromatic stable homotopy theory
            and from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            are given in (
            %a{:href => "#Greenlees16"}> Greenlees16, Sec. 23
            ).
